# 12. Lists + Tuples + Sets Together

Real programs often combine data structures.

Example:

```python
developers = [
    ("Amit", "Backend"),
    ("Rahul", "Frontend"),
    ("Priya", "Backend"),
    ("Neha", "DevOps")
]

active = {"Amit", "Priya", "Neha"}
```

We can use tuple unpacking:

```python
for name, role in developers:
    if name in active:
        print(name, role)
```

We can use a set to collect unique roles:

```python
roles = set()

for name, role in developers:
    if name in active:
        roles.add(role)

print(roles)
```

This combines:

```text
List
 ↓
Tuple
 ↓
Set membership
 ↓
Condition
 ↓
Set for unique results
```

This is the type of data-processing logic you should become comfortable with.

