# 17. Dictionary vs Other Data Structures

| Feature    | List     | Tuple      | Set         | Dictionary                 |
| ---------- | -------- | ---------- | ----------- | -------------------------- |
| Ordered    | ✅        | ✅          | ❌           | Insertion order preserved* |
| Mutable    | ✅        | ❌          | ✅           | ✅                          |
| Duplicates | ✅        | ✅          | ❌           | Keys ❌ / Values ✅          |
| Indexing   | ✅        | ✅          | ❌           | ❌                          |
| Access     | Index    | Index      | Membership  | Key                        |
| Main use   | Sequence | Fixed data | Unique data | Key → Value                |

*Modern Python dictionaries preserve insertion order, but you should think of them primarily as **key-value mappings**, not as indexed sequences.

